Title: [Help wanted] Spring Boot - TestContainers - Simple BearerToken?

This is probably a super simple issue but I just don't understand the documentation that exists on mock-ouath2-server, really need help...

What I want to do is just to set up a very simple security validation for my Spring Boot application, to begin with. Where no user detail would need to be provided by the client, just a request to the auth server from the client to get a valid bearer token that can pass the validation step that Spring Boot requires.

**Server**
application.yaml:
```
spring:
  security:
    oauth2:
      resourceserver:
        jwt:
          issuer-set-uri: http://localhost:8080/default
          jwk-set-uri: http://localhost:8080/default/jwks
```
As I figured I don't need any customization as of yet I'm using the default beans for security so my security config is just a shell for now:
```
@Configuration
@EnableWebFluxSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {}
```
**Test module**
My TestContainer that wraps the mock-ouath2-server image looks like this (belongs to same network as the Application container):
```
public class AuthorizationContainer extends GenericContainer<AuthorizationContainer> {
    private static final DockerImageName AUTHORIZATION_IMAGE = DockerImageName.parse("ghcr.io/navikt/mock-oauth2-server:2.0.0");
    private static final int APP_PORT = 8080;
    public AuthorizationContainer() {
        super(AUTHORIZATION_IMAGE );

        addFixedExposedPort(APP_PORT, APP_PORT);
        waitingFor(Wait.forHttp("/isalive").forStatusCode(200));
    }
}
```
**How do you create a valid bearer token with this setup?**

